module System

### Represents the crashable raised when code tries to consume an absent optional
### result as though a value were present.
crashable AbsentValueError
    pass

### Represents the crashable used when program execution is terminated by the
### user or hosting environment.
crashable UserTerminationError
    pass

### Represents the crashable raised when a runtime verification check fails.
### This is used by generic verification surfaces that enforce invariants and
### preconditions explicitly.
crashable VerificationFailedError
    pass

### Represents the crashable raised when code reaches a state that should be
### impossible if surrounding logic is correct.
crashable LogicBreachedError
    pass

### Represents the crashable raised when a lookup cannot find a requested key.
crashable KeyNotFoundError
    ### Stores the key that could not be resolved.
    key: Text

### Raised when an Agent's work could not be started (thread or allocation failure).
crashable TaskSpawnError
    pass

### Raised when an Agent is started a second time, or started with `start_here()` inside a `start_now()` job
### (which can move between threads, so it has no thread of its own to run a job beside).
crashable AgentStartError
    ### What went wrong.
    reason: Text

### Raised when an Agent that was cancelled is retrieved: its work stopped, or never ran, so it has no value.
### Cancelling is not a failure, which is why the name carries no `Error`.
crashable CancelRequested
    pass

### Raised when an Agent's work did not finish before its `waitfor` deadline.
crashable TaskTimeoutError
    pass

### Raised when transmitting to a channel that has been closed, or whose every consumer has gone — the item
### can never be delivered. Closing itself is not an error (it is the normal end-of-stream signal);
### only a `transmit` after close is.
crashable ChannelClosedError
    pass

### Raised when an agent opens access to a `Guarded` it already has open, in a routine called from inside the block
### that opened it. Waiting would never end (the block can't end while the agent waits), and letting it in would show
### the block's work half done, so the program stops.
crashable ReenterDuringAccessError
    pass

### Raised by a `viewing` / `modifying` block when two of its targets are the same entity under two names: the two
### tokens it hands out are taken to be two different entities, so one can be changed while the other's element is
### held.
crashable AliasedTokensError
    pass

### Returns the default message for two tokens asked on the same entity.
### :returns: The resulting `Text` value.
@readonly
@override
routine AliasedTokensError.crash_message() -> Text
    return "Two names this block opens are the same entity. Opening it twice would give two tokens on one entity, so a change through one could move what the other reads. Name it once."

### Raised by `steal` on a `Retained` or `Guarded` handle that is not the only strong handle: taking the entity out
### would leave the other holders pointing at nothing.
crashable SharedHandleStealError
    ### How many strong handles shared the entity, the stolen one included.
    holders: U64

### Returns the default message for a `steal` of a shared handle.
### :returns: The resulting `Text` value.
@readonly
@override
routine SharedHandleStealError.crash_message() -> Text
    return f"steal takes the entity out of a handle only when that handle is the last one, but {me.holders} handles share it. Drop the other handles first, or keep the handle and read through it."

### Returns the default message for absent-value failures.
### :returns: The resulting `Text` value.
@readonly
@override
routine AbsentValueError.crash_message() -> Text
    return "Attempted to access a value that is absent."

### Returns the default message for user-requested termination.
### :returns: The resulting `Text` value.
@readonly
@override
routine UserTerminationError.crash_message() -> Text
    return "Program was stopped by user."

### Returns the default message for verification failures.
### :returns: The resulting `Text` value.
@readonly
@override
routine VerificationFailedError.crash_message() -> Text
    return "A verification check failed."

### Returns the default message for breached logic invariants.
### :returns: The resulting `Text` value.
@readonly
@override
routine LogicBreachedError.crash_message() -> Text
    return "A logic breach was detected."

### Returns the default message for failed keyed lookup.
### :returns: The resulting `Text` value.
@readonly
@override
routine KeyNotFoundError.crash_message() -> Text
    return f"Key not found: {me.key}"

### Returns the default message for task-spawn failures.
### :returns: The resulting `Text` value.
@readonly
@override
routine TaskSpawnError.crash_message() -> Text
    return "The agent could not be started."

### Returns the default message for a cancelled Agent.
### :returns: The resulting `Text` value.
@readonly
@override
routine CancelRequested.crash_message() -> Text
    return "The agent was cancelled, so it has no value."

### Returns the reason the Agent could not start.
### :returns: The resulting `Text` value.
@readonly
@override
routine AgentStartError.crash_message() -> Text
    return me.reason

### Returns the default message for task-timeout failures.
### :returns: The resulting `Text` value.
@readonly
@override
routine TaskTimeoutError.crash_message() -> Text
    return "Threaded task did not finish before its deadline."

### Returns the default message for transmitting to a closed channel.
### :returns: The resulting `Text` value.
@readonly
@override
routine ChannelClosedError.crash_message() -> Text
    return "Cannot transmit to a closed channel (no consumer can receive the item)."

### Returns the default message for opening a `Guarded` again from inside the block that has it open.
### :returns: The resulting `Text` value.
@readonly
@override
routine ReenterDuringAccessError.crash_message() -> Text
    return "This agent opens access to a Guarded it already has open. Waiting for it would never end, and going in would see the work of its own block half done. Pass the token you already have instead of opening it again."
